+## Generated Git files
+
+Git-backed reviews hide paths when Git resolves `linguist-generated` as `set`
+or `true`. Explicit `false`, unset attributes, and unspecified paths stay visible.
+Git resolves nested `.gitattributes` rules and its normal attribute precedence;
+Hunk does not maintain a separate ignore file.
+
+Use `--include-generated` when those paths need review:
+
+```bash
+hunk diff --include-generated
+hunk diff --staged --include-generated
+hunk show HEAD --include-generated
+hunk stash show --include-generated
+```
+
+Working-tree reviews use working-tree attributes with Git's index fallback.
+Staged reviews use index attributes. Commit and range reviews use the right/new
+revision, including the destination path for renames. Deleted paths use the
+old revision or index. Stash reviews use the stash snapshot and its first parent.
+Git's local and global attribute overrides still apply.
+
+The choice survives reload, `hunk resume`, and watch refreshes. A new review
+command defaults to hiding generated paths unless it includes the flag.
+Attribute lookup failures keep files visible and report one bounded warning.
+Git versions without `check-attr --source` fail open for revision attributes;
+upgrade Git or use `--include-generated` to skip the lookup.
+
+Patch, concrete-file, difftool, Jujutsu, and Sapling inputs do not use this filter.
